Subject: [PATCH] server: Save the registry periodically on Android.

Proton dropped Wine's periodic registry save; the server only saves when
it exits. Android ends apps with SIGKILL (force stop, swiping the app
away, low memory), so the server rarely exits on its own and registry
changes were lost: wine.inf's font entries after a prefix update, which
left DirectWrite without Tahoma and crashed Steam's web UI, as well as
anything programs store there. Save every 30 seconds, as upstream Wine
does.
---
--- a/server/registry.c
+++ b/server/registry.c
@@ -1890,6 +1890,17 @@ static void init_supported_machines(void)
     native_machine = supported_machines[0];
 }
 
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+/* Android ends apps with SIGKILL (force stop, swiping the app away, low memory),
+ * so the server rarely gets to save the registry when it exits; save it
+ * every 30 seconds, as upstream Wine does */
+static void periodic_save( void *arg )
+{
+    flush_registry();
+    add_timeout_user( -30 * (timeout_t)TICKS_PER_SEC, periodic_save, NULL );
+}
+#endif
+
 /* registry initialisation */
 void init_registry(void)
 {
@@ -2029,6 +2040,10 @@ void init_registry(void)
 
     /* go back to the server dir */
     if (fchdir( server_dir_fd ) == -1) fatal_error( "chdir to server dir: %s\n", strerror( errno ));
+
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+    add_timeout_user( -30 * (timeout_t)TICKS_PER_SEC, periodic_save, NULL );
+#endif
 }
 
 /* save a registry branch to a file */
